1
00:02:21,759 --> 00:02:23,840
Attack! Push, push! Here they come!

2
00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:24,520
Go!

3
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:25,800
Push!

4
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:27,560
Hit him!

5
00:02:34,639 --> 00:02:35,319
Uncle Qi.

6
00:02:36,639 --> 00:02:38,280
Since when does vocational school offer gaming classes,

7
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:39,560
and hold them in an internet cafe?

8
00:02:40,479 --> 00:02:41,360
Uncle Qi...

9
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:43,080
I just got here.

10
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:44,240
I've only been sitting here for ten minutes.

11
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:45,800
The computer tower isn't even warm yet.

12
00:02:46,159 --> 00:02:46,879
Really!

13
00:02:46,879 --> 00:02:48,520
Are there wolves and dogs at school?

14
00:02:48,639 --> 00:02:49,599
Are they going to bite you?

15
00:02:49,599 --> 00:02:50,479
You just can't stay put.

16
00:02:50,479 --> 00:02:51,520
I'll go back right now.

17
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:55,800
Have you eaten?

18
00:02:56,080 --> 00:02:56,719
Not yet.

19
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:14,319
Don't waste it.

20
00:03:14,599 --> 00:03:15,719
Thanks, Uncle Qi.

21
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:17,199
Your mom's on a business trip.

22
00:03:17,199 --> 00:03:17,879
A long one.

23
00:03:17,879 --> 00:03:19,199
She won't be back anytime soon.

24
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:21,159
Call me anytime if anything comes up.

25
00:03:21,639 --> 00:03:22,800
You remember both numbers, right?

26
00:03:23,199 --> 00:03:23,840
I do.

27
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:24,680
Recite them for me.

28
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:25,520
No need.

29
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:27,039
I won't forget your number.

30
00:03:30,719 --> 00:03:32,680
When is my dad coming back?

31
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:35,599
Did my mom go looking for him?

32
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:39,120
There are rules. I can't say.

33
00:03:41,639 --> 00:03:42,759
I don't really care.

34
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:44,280
Grandpa keeps asking.

35
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:45,879
And I can't lie to him.

36
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:47,639
He keeps telling me to call.

37
00:03:48,240 --> 00:03:49,400
It's driving me crazy.

38
00:04:01,719 --> 00:04:02,840
Welcome.

39
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:05,719
Welcome to the Pacific Nightclub.

40
00:04:05,719 --> 00:04:06,400
Brother Qi.

41
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:08,159
Let's go.

42
00:04:09,439 --> 00:04:10,800
Let's wait and go in with Brother Xiao.

43
00:04:11,599 --> 00:04:13,240
We don't have to apologize if we don't wait, do we?

44
00:04:15,719 --> 00:04:16,759
Welcome.

45
00:04:17,319 --> 00:04:20,480
Welcome to the Pacific Nightclub.

46
00:04:23,639 --> 00:04:27,079
Welcome to the Pacific Nightclub.

47
00:04:40,879 --> 00:04:42,399
You sang so well!

48
00:04:42,399 --> 00:04:45,160
Others can only sing, not dance,

49
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:47,720
but no one sings and dances like you,

50
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:49,040
and dances so well at that.

51
00:04:50,639 --> 00:04:51,759
You're quite the flatterer.

52
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:52,519
I mean it!

53
00:04:52,519 --> 00:04:53,720
I never lie to you.

54
00:04:53,720 --> 00:04:54,800
You know that.

55
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:57,079
Xiao Jin contacted me this afternoon,

56
00:04:57,079 --> 00:04:58,160
asking for a few days off

57
00:04:58,160 --> 00:04:59,319
to get some rest.

58
00:04:59,319 --> 00:05:01,160
I said a few days isn't nearly enough.

59
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:02,879
If she's resting, she should take good care

60
00:05:02,879 --> 00:05:03,800
and recover properly.

61
00:05:03,879 --> 00:05:06,920
Otherwise, won't she just become your headache?

62
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:08,680
What do you mean, "my headache"?

63
00:05:08,879 --> 00:05:10,240
Don't I have enough trouble as it is?

64
00:05:10,879 --> 00:05:11,800
No,

65
00:05:12,959 --> 00:05:14,959
I remember Brother Qi saying before

66
00:05:14,959 --> 00:05:15,839
that once people

67
00:05:15,839 --> 00:05:18,360
reach middle age, it's not like when they were young.

68
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:20,120
Troubles are like candied haws on a skewer—

69
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:21,279
one right after another,

70
00:05:21,279 --> 00:05:22,319
and you have to swallow them all.

71
00:05:22,319 --> 00:05:24,360
Whether she comes has nothing to do with me.

72
00:05:24,759 --> 00:05:26,160
I don't even know where she is.

73
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:27,879
Isn't that just how the girls are?

74
00:05:27,879 --> 00:05:29,639
Out with the old, in with the new.

75
00:05:30,319 --> 00:05:30,959
Gentlemen,

76
00:05:30,959 --> 00:05:32,920
we have a few new girls today,

77
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:34,360
all on their very first day.

78
00:05:34,680 --> 00:05:35,079
Bro,

79
00:05:36,319 --> 00:05:37,040
Brother Qi.

80
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:39,399
All right, sort them out.

81
00:05:39,399 --> 00:05:39,839
All right, all right.

82
00:05:39,839 --> 00:05:40,720
I'm on it.

83
00:05:40,959 --> 00:05:41,399
Now then,

84
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:42,920
don't just stand there.

85
00:05:43,319 --> 00:05:44,240
Go over and take a seat.

86
00:05:44,639 --> 00:05:46,319
Learn some drinking games.

87
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:48,759
I'll leave you gentlemen to it.

88
00:05:48,879 --> 00:05:49,879
Got work to do.

89
00:05:49,879 --> 00:05:51,000
Call me if you need anything.

90
00:05:51,639 --> 00:05:52,319
Gentlemen,

91
00:05:52,319 --> 00:05:54,079
what kind of songs do you usually like?

92
00:05:54,079 --> 00:05:55,680
I know, I know!

93
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:56,279
All right.

94
00:05:56,279 --> 00:05:57,319
Wait.

95
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:01,680
Director Hao has a surgery and will be late.

96
00:06:02,120 --> 00:06:03,720
Let's get down to business before he arrives.

97
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:04,720
On the morning of the third,

98
00:06:04,720 --> 00:06:06,720
we're meeting the secretary of Gulou District Hospital.

99
00:06:06,720 --> 00:06:08,519
We still have disagreements over what we discussed last time.

100
00:06:08,519 --> 00:06:09,319
We can't put it off any longer.

101
00:06:09,319 --> 00:06:10,240
Let's settle it today.

102
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:11,519
The sooner we decide, the sooner we can relax.

103
00:06:11,519 --> 00:06:12,839
You think we should act as the agent for Neusoft's

104
00:06:12,839 --> 00:06:13,920
Computed Tomography scanner sales.

105
00:06:13,920 --> 00:06:15,120
I've thought about it for days,

106
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:17,439
and I think we should secure the maintenance contracts first.

107
00:06:17,759 --> 00:06:19,120
It's just like property management.

108
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:20,639
It's a steady meal ticket.

109
00:06:21,040 --> 00:06:23,240
Even brand-new machines need maintenance, after all.

110
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:24,240
Leasing, repairs, operations...

111
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:25,680
Wouldn't it be great to expand across the board?

112
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:26,959
Doing both...

113
00:06:26,959 --> 00:06:28,399
Couldn't that work too?

114
00:06:28,399 --> 00:06:29,959
After all, we're not short on cash.

115
00:06:29,959 --> 00:06:31,800
Our cash flow is indeed fine.

116
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:33,720
But doing business requires logic.

117
00:06:33,720 --> 00:06:34,160
When it comes to Computed Tomography scanners,

118
00:06:34,160 --> 00:06:34,959
as a business,

119
00:06:34,959 --> 00:06:37,360
it's not the time for blind expansion yet.

120
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:38,839
Don't bite off more than you can chew.

121
00:06:38,839 --> 00:06:40,279
Cultivate deeply and carefully,

122
00:06:40,279 --> 00:06:41,160
just like you said,

123
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:42,000
right?

124
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:43,000
Sure,

125
00:06:44,199 --> 00:06:45,680
but Brother Qi, listen to me.

126
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:47,720
China's economy is like a dragon.

127
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:49,199
Now that the dragon has raised its head,

128
00:06:49,199 --> 00:06:50,560
it's ready to soar at any moment.

129
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:52,439
Nobody can stop it.

130
00:06:52,439 --> 00:06:53,560
I don't think any hospital

131
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:55,439
will lease machines anymore.

132
00:06:55,439 --> 00:06:57,360
Once you have money, who still wears old shoes?

133
00:06:57,360 --> 00:06:58,680
Of course they'll buy new ones.

134
00:06:58,959 --> 00:07:00,160
I used to think so, too.

135
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:02,240
But have we been on business trips to the north?

136
00:07:02,680 --> 00:07:04,279
We need data to back up our arguments.

137
00:07:04,920 --> 00:07:05,759
You've seen it yourself.

138
00:07:05,759 --> 00:07:06,680
China is so vast.

139
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:08,199
For the exact same county hospital,

140
00:07:08,199 --> 00:07:10,480
in the south, 100 million a year is considered poor,

141
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:12,079
while in the north, it's three million a year,

142
00:07:12,079 --> 00:07:14,600
and their director is already getting promoted.

143
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:16,199
Do you see my point?

144
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:18,759
Alright, alright.

145
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:19,480
How about this?

146
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:20,720
Let's take a democratic vote, okay?

147
00:07:20,959 --> 00:07:22,000
Three of us, one vote each.

148
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:23,079
That way, there'll be a clear decision.

149
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:24,160
The two of us each cast a vote,

150
00:07:24,160 --> 00:07:25,279
and now it's up to you.

151
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:43,680
I vote for you.

152
00:07:47,800 --> 00:07:48,480
That's that.

153
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:49,800
Business is done. I have nothing more to say.

154
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:50,399
Let's drink.

155
00:07:51,439 --> 00:07:53,560
I get what Brother Xiao means.

156
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:56,240
Let's run a pilot first to see how it works.

157
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:56,639
Right?

158
00:07:56,639 --> 00:07:58,439
If it fails, we do as Brother Qi said.

159
00:07:58,439 --> 00:07:59,439
We go with property management.

160
00:07:59,439 --> 00:08:00,240
Sound good?

161
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:02,839
It's just business.

162
00:08:02,839 --> 00:08:04,199
We're not here to make friends.

163
00:08:04,199 --> 00:08:05,680
We should lay everything on the table.

164
00:08:05,680 --> 00:08:07,240
From my first day with Brother Qi,

165
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:08,319
he taught me that.

166
00:08:08,319 --> 00:08:09,000
Hold it right there.

167
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:10,519
Don't you dare say that.

168
00:08:10,519 --> 00:08:12,000
How could I teach you?

169
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:13,360
Who am I to teach you?

170
00:08:14,519 --> 00:08:16,480
Couldn't, wouldn't, and never did.

171
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:20,439
What's going on?

172
00:08:20,759 --> 00:08:22,680
Drunk before we even started?

173
00:08:22,680 --> 00:08:24,160
Still haven't slept off lunch?

174
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:24,639
Hurry, hurry.

175
00:08:24,920 --> 00:08:26,120
Pour Brother Qi some hot tea.

176
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:26,560
Right away!

177
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:28,680
When I say I don't dare, I mean it.

178
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:29,800
Brother He Chunxiao,

179
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:31,120
I'm not joking.

180
00:08:31,120 --> 00:08:32,559
Don't ever say that again.

181
00:08:32,879 --> 00:08:35,120
My shoulders aren't broad enough to carry that.

182
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:45,279
Brother Qi,

183
00:08:45,519 --> 00:08:46,879
please don't hold it against me.

184
00:08:47,399 --> 00:08:48,519
I was out of line.

185
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:50,679
From the day you took me under your wing,

186
00:08:50,679 --> 00:08:51,600
you've known

187
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:54,360
I'm slow and disappointing.

188
00:08:54,679 --> 00:08:55,720
Everything you taught me,

189
00:08:56,039 --> 00:08:57,240
look how I handled it.

190
00:08:58,279 --> 00:08:59,919
You know who I am, right?

191
00:08:59,919 --> 00:09:01,919
What does who you are have to do with me?

192
00:09:01,919 --> 00:09:03,200
Nothing at all.

193
00:09:04,039 --> 00:09:04,960
If you think I'm wrong,

194
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:05,799
that my judgment is flawed,

195
00:09:05,799 --> 00:09:06,639
that's your problem.

196
00:09:06,639 --> 00:09:07,720
There's nothing wrong with me.

197
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:08,600
Let me repeat this.

198
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:10,399
My issues have nothing to do with you.

199
00:09:10,399 --> 00:09:11,399
You are you, and I am me.

200
00:09:11,399 --> 00:09:12,399
Don't lump us together.

201
00:09:12,399 --> 00:09:14,200
Don't ever drag me into your mess, got it?

202
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:20,360
All right, all right.

203
00:09:21,279 --> 00:09:23,000
Let's drop it and have a drink.

204
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:25,159
Right? We're doing business together.

205
00:09:25,159 --> 00:09:26,399
Hands off. Don't touch me.

206
00:09:26,399 --> 00:09:27,360
Don't get me wrong.

207
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:28,840
I'm not talking about the vote.

208
00:09:29,159 --> 00:09:31,000
I'm talking about basic decency.

209
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,919
You shouldn't be so mercenary in life.

210
00:09:32,919 --> 00:09:34,639
You cling to me when you need me,

211
00:09:34,639 --> 00:09:36,159
and turn on me when you don't.

212
00:09:36,159 --> 00:09:37,519
Did I teach you that too?

213
00:09:38,799 --> 00:09:40,679
What, feeling wronged?

214
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:42,879
If you're that sensitive, don't come out.

215
00:09:43,320 --> 00:09:44,240
Don't you get it?

216
00:09:47,559 --> 00:09:49,519
To tell you the truth,

217
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:51,879
I envy Brother Xiao the most.

218
00:09:52,519 --> 00:09:53,639
If only, growing up,

219
00:09:53,639 --> 00:09:55,559
I had someone like Brother Qi around,

220
00:09:55,559 --> 00:09:57,480
what's that idiom again?

221
00:09:57,480 --> 00:09:59,840
"Hard advice is tough to swallow."

222
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:00,919
If I'd had that kind of discipline,

223
00:10:00,919 --> 00:10:02,960
life wouldn't have beaten me down so much.

224
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:03,519
All right, all right.

225
00:10:03,519 --> 00:10:04,759
Come to the restroom with me.

226
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:05,960
Take a leak.

227
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:07,840
Tell me what else Brother Qi taught you.

228
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:09,799
Don't just sit here like a log.

229
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:11,279
Have a drink with Brother Qi!

230
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:11,960
Brother,

231
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:13,639
let me pour you a drink, Brother.

232
00:10:13,759 --> 00:10:15,080
Brother, what songs do you like to listen to?

233
00:10:15,080 --> 00:10:15,840
I'll sing one for you.

234
00:10:28,799 --> 00:10:31,120
Selena, Selena.

235
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:32,320
Let us go.

236
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:34,639
Let's go, back to the room.

237
00:11:42,799 --> 00:11:43,679
Brother Qi.

238
00:11:44,279 --> 00:11:45,360
Heading home, or somewhere else?

239
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:48,279
Where do you think I'm going?

240
00:11:48,679 --> 00:11:50,200
Didn't you go to the hospital last time?

241
00:11:51,039 --> 00:11:52,000
No need to go lately?

242
00:11:53,639 --> 00:11:55,600
Even if you leave tomorrow,

243
00:11:55,600 --> 00:11:57,080
we're still partners today.

244
00:11:57,440 --> 00:11:59,200
Even if we're not on the same task force later,

245
00:11:59,480 --> 00:12:00,759
just let me know if you need anything.

246
00:12:01,159 --> 00:12:02,279
Don't be so petty.

247
00:12:02,799 --> 00:12:04,000
You taught me:

248
00:12:09,279 --> 00:12:11,000
laugh it off.

249
00:12:11,799 --> 00:12:13,000
You're not angry at all.

250
00:12:13,519 --> 00:12:15,440
I've been slow my whole life.

251
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:16,919
I could never master anything,

252
00:12:17,240 --> 00:12:18,519
but I remembered one thing:

253
00:12:19,159 --> 00:12:19,960
don't get angry.

254
00:12:20,120 --> 00:12:21,240
Because it's useless.

255
00:12:21,559 --> 00:12:23,879
There are plenty of setbacks and worries.

256
00:12:24,240 --> 00:12:26,200
Nobody's life is smooth sailing.

257
00:12:26,279 --> 00:12:28,399
Plenty of indignities, too. So,

258
00:12:28,639 --> 00:12:30,440
anger is the most pointless thing there is.

259
00:12:30,759 --> 00:12:33,000
Sometimes, emotions are like a blade.

260
00:12:33,519 --> 00:12:34,440
It either stabs someone else,

261
00:12:34,840 --> 00:12:35,759
or it stabs yourself.

262
00:12:36,559 --> 00:12:37,759
Old Wei told me that.

263
00:12:38,279 --> 00:12:39,960
Back then, when you were wrongly blamed,

264
00:12:39,960 --> 00:12:42,120
weren't you the one sharpening knives in rage?

265
00:12:44,360 --> 00:12:45,600
Thanks to you reminding me

266
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:47,320
that being in State Security means taking grievances.

267
00:12:47,639 --> 00:12:48,440
If not for you,

268
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:49,360
I wouldn't even remember.

269
00:12:56,559 --> 00:12:57,279
Good.

270
00:12:58,080 --> 00:12:59,879
There's nothing left for me to teach you.

271
00:13:00,200 --> 00:13:01,360
You're doing great already.

272
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:04,039
For the next couple of days, at least,

273
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:05,240
you still need to teach me.

274
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:06,879
Teach what?

275
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:08,440
Interrogation.

276
00:13:08,840 --> 00:13:10,879
How long do you plan to leave A-Cai hanging?

277
00:13:50,080 --> 00:13:51,200
Long time no see.

278
00:13:52,279 --> 00:13:53,559
Didn't we just see each other?

279
00:15:24,879 --> 00:15:25,320
Hello, President Lin.

280
00:15:25,320 --> 00:15:25,559
President Lin.

281
00:15:30,039 --> 00:15:30,799
President Lin.

282
00:16:14,919 --> 00:16:17,320
If you suddenly find in your home

283
00:16:18,360 --> 00:16:20,000
any unusual traces,

284
00:16:20,320 --> 00:16:23,279
it's very likely a warning sign.

285
00:16:24,039 --> 00:16:25,639
You must be on high alert immediately.

286
00:17:09,039 --> 00:17:10,880
Don't worry, everyone. Nothing's going to happen.

287
00:17:10,880 --> 00:17:12,799
Sister Xia, we aren't shutting down, are we?

288
00:17:12,799 --> 00:17:14,079
Yeah, we're not going bust, right?

289
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:15,200
You bunch of jinxes!

290
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:16,519
Watch what you say, all of you!

291
00:17:16,519 --> 00:17:17,559
It's nothing serious.

292
00:17:17,559 --> 00:17:19,599
We just had some issues with the fire inspection.

293
00:17:19,599 --> 00:17:21,720
I'll go smooth things over with them.

294
00:17:21,720 --> 00:17:22,559
We'll reopen in a few days.

295
00:17:22,559 --> 00:17:23,839
Just take a break for the next few days.

296
00:17:23,839 --> 00:17:25,440
You always complain you're too exhausted to sleep.

297
00:17:25,440 --> 00:17:26,640
Now that you get to rest, you're not happy?

298
00:17:26,640 --> 00:17:27,359
But if you're closed,

299
00:17:27,359 --> 00:17:28,559
where do we go tonight?

300
00:17:28,559 --> 00:17:29,039
Exactly.

301
00:17:29,039 --> 00:17:30,240
Come crash at my place.

302
00:17:30,400 --> 00:17:31,119
You're so useless.

303
00:17:31,119 --> 00:17:33,200
All this time and you can't even lock down a man.

304
00:17:34,039 --> 00:17:34,680
Sis.

305
00:17:35,480 --> 00:17:36,799
I need to ask you something.

306
00:17:38,039 --> 00:17:38,839
What is it?

307
00:17:39,559 --> 00:17:42,759
Could I get an advance on my pay?

308
00:17:43,759 --> 00:17:45,319
Didn't you just get paid a couple of days ago?

309
00:17:45,319 --> 00:17:46,319
Where's your money?

310
00:17:47,079 --> 00:17:48,559
I want to rent a place.

311
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:54,799
I don't want your personal money.

312
00:17:54,799 --> 00:17:55,279
It's all the same.

313
00:17:55,279 --> 00:17:57,160
Really, just an advance on my salary is fine.

314
00:17:57,160 --> 00:17:57,920
Just take it for now.

315
00:17:57,920 --> 00:17:58,799
Manager!

316
00:17:59,160 --> 00:17:59,799
Come here for a second.

317
00:18:00,119 --> 00:18:00,799
Coming!

318
00:18:01,079 --> 00:18:01,759
Wait for me a second.

319
00:18:01,759 --> 00:18:02,480
Okay.

320
00:18:02,759 --> 00:18:03,640
Sir, sir!

321
00:18:03,640 --> 00:18:04,680
Coming, coming. What's wrong?

322
00:18:05,640 --> 00:18:07,400
Here is the temporary closure decision.

323
00:18:08,240 --> 00:18:09,119
Wait, no...

324
00:18:09,119 --> 00:18:12,200
How long are we being penalized for?

325
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:13,599
Ten days for now.

326
00:18:13,599 --> 00:18:15,880
If you don't rectify it, it could be permanent.

327
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:16,680
Rectify, yes, we'll rectify!

328
00:18:16,680 --> 00:18:17,880
We'll definitely fix it, definitely!

329
00:18:18,960 --> 00:18:20,400
You wouldn't pick up your phone to save your life!

330
00:18:21,960 --> 00:18:23,759
What are you messing around with out there all day?

331
00:18:24,680 --> 00:18:25,880
What did I even do?

332
00:18:26,640 --> 00:18:28,519
You barely send any money home either.

333
00:18:28,799 --> 00:18:30,519
Are you someone's mistress?

334
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:31,920
Speak up!

335
00:18:32,519 --> 00:18:34,319
Are you doing something shameful?

336
00:18:34,519 --> 00:18:35,880
You don't even dare to come home!

337
00:18:37,079 --> 00:18:39,079
Emergency exits, evacuation routes...

338
00:18:39,480 --> 00:18:41,000
Clear out everything that needs clearing.

339
00:18:41,079 --> 00:18:42,079
Hello, Boss Zhao.

340
00:18:42,160 --> 00:18:42,880
Yes, yes, right.

341
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:44,720
It's Xiao Xia. It's Xiao Xia.

342
00:18:44,720 --> 00:18:46,319
Operating during rectification is not permitted.

343
00:18:46,319 --> 00:18:47,799
We're having a fire inspection right now,

344
00:18:48,359 --> 00:18:49,680
and they told me to wait for notice.

345
00:18:51,039 --> 00:18:51,680
Yes, exactly.

346
00:18:51,680 --> 00:18:53,599
Well, you know, if we...

347
00:18:53,599 --> 00:18:55,279
If this gets shut down, how do I answer for it?

348
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:27,000
This name of yours...

349
00:19:27,559 --> 00:19:28,359
sounds like a pen name,

350
00:19:29,599 --> 00:19:30,519
like a poet's.

351
00:19:47,039 --> 00:19:48,759
I'm a friend of Li Fengge.

352
00:19:48,759 --> 00:19:49,920
She sent me to see you.

353
00:19:52,359 --> 00:19:53,400
What's wrong with her?

354
00:19:54,960 --> 00:19:55,720
She's sick.

355
00:19:56,359 --> 00:19:58,440
She's been an accountant at a travel agency.

356
00:19:58,680 --> 00:19:59,200
A recent medical checkup...

357
00:19:59,200 --> 00:20:01,039
I've been praying she'd get sick.

358
00:20:01,359 --> 00:20:02,440
Best if she never recovers.

359
00:20:06,720 --> 00:20:08,799
She told me last time that you needed help.

360
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:12,279
I need a job.

361
00:20:14,640 --> 00:20:16,480
I'll get you into the travel agency soon.

362
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:19,759
What do you need me to do?

363
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:23,880
Nothing.

364
00:20:26,079 --> 00:20:27,359
You don't have to pretend.

365
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:30,200
It's all a transaction. I get it.

366
00:20:50,880 --> 00:20:51,960
You know what?

367
00:20:53,119 --> 00:20:54,400
I went to see her today.

368
00:20:55,319 --> 00:20:56,079
I feel like...

369
00:20:56,079 --> 00:20:56,960
Sister-in-law!

370
00:20:57,759 --> 00:20:58,559
You're back.

371
00:21:00,400 --> 00:21:01,319
Boss Lin.

372
00:21:02,759 --> 00:21:03,880
He always says you're busy.

373
00:21:04,079 --> 00:21:05,799
Didn't expect you to be working this late.

374
00:21:05,799 --> 00:21:07,400
So dedicated right after getting married.

375
00:21:07,400 --> 00:21:09,599
No wonder your business is thriving.

376
00:21:11,240 --> 00:21:11,799
All right, then.

377
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:13,200
The wife is home,

378
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:14,839
so I know when to leave. I'll take off.

379
00:21:14,839 --> 00:21:16,640
It's fine, have a couple more drinks.

380
00:21:16,640 --> 00:21:17,400
No need.

381
00:21:17,400 --> 00:21:18,680
We can always drink another time.

382
00:21:22,599 --> 00:21:24,160
You've been to so many places,

383
00:21:25,240 --> 00:21:26,519
but never to Taiwan, China.

384
00:21:26,920 --> 00:21:28,359
I hope I can visit someday.

385
00:21:40,839 --> 00:21:41,599
Definitely.

386
00:21:42,440 --> 00:21:43,720
There'll definitely be a chance.

387
00:21:44,640 --> 00:21:46,359
Alishan, Sun Moon Lake,

388
00:21:46,359 --> 00:21:47,559
Keelung, Kenting...

389
00:21:47,559 --> 00:21:48,640
Go wherever you like.

390
00:21:48,799 --> 00:21:49,759
It's all on me.

391
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:50,680
It's a deal.

392
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:52,319
Then when the time comes, we can

393
00:21:52,319 --> 00:21:53,720
drink nine rounds down Zhongxiao East Road.

394
00:21:54,039 --> 00:21:55,640
If you say so, it's a sure thing.

395
00:21:58,400 --> 00:21:59,920
Take it from me.

396
00:22:00,160 --> 00:22:02,519
You and Brother Qi are both doing this for the project.

397
00:22:02,640 --> 00:22:04,599
A little friction is totally normal.

398
00:22:04,839 --> 00:22:06,799
There's nothing a drink can't fix.

399
00:22:06,799 --> 00:22:07,440
Let's go.

400
00:22:08,720 --> 00:22:09,720
We're heading out, sister-in-law.

401
00:22:22,279 --> 00:22:23,000
Here's your rouyan.

402
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:28,119
What're you thinking? Watch where you're going.

403
00:22:28,119 --> 00:22:29,680
You almost spilled hot soup on my shoes.

404
00:22:30,480 --> 00:22:31,799
What else could I be thinking about?

405
00:22:31,920 --> 00:22:32,759
One bowl of rouyan.

406
00:22:32,759 --> 00:22:35,039
That suspect in the interrogation room is all I can think about.

407
00:22:35,359 --> 00:22:37,119
Now that you're washing your hands of it,

408
00:22:37,240 --> 00:22:39,759
how can a nobody like me get him to talk?

409
00:22:39,759 --> 00:22:40,839
I was so stressed I couldn't sleep all night.

410
00:22:40,839 --> 00:22:42,160
Here, your rouyan.

411
00:22:43,079 --> 00:22:43,680
Enjoy your meal.

412
00:22:44,960 --> 00:22:45,640
What about you?

413
00:22:45,960 --> 00:22:47,359
Looks like you've got dark circles too.

414
00:22:47,519 --> 00:22:48,680
Couldn't sleep either?

415
00:22:50,160 --> 00:22:51,559
Depends on where you're staying up.

416
00:22:53,359 --> 00:22:54,839
Spending the night in a hospital room,

417
00:22:54,839 --> 00:22:56,160
you might as well not have slept at all.

418
00:23:00,119 --> 00:23:02,640
You usually have two eggs,

419
00:23:02,640 --> 00:23:04,519
a fried cruller, and a bowl of rouyan.

420
00:23:04,519 --> 00:23:06,480
When you're in a good mood, you even add a pancake.

421
00:23:06,480 --> 00:23:07,240
What's up today?

422
00:23:07,240 --> 00:23:08,240
Something on your mind?

423
00:23:08,240 --> 00:23:10,160
I ate even more when I first joined the department.

424
00:23:10,759 --> 00:23:11,960
Back then, I thought

425
00:23:11,960 --> 00:23:13,400
people's appetites just shrink with age.

426
00:23:13,519 --> 00:23:15,160
Turns out, it's because you have more weighing on your mind.

427
00:23:15,160 --> 00:23:16,759
All the blood rushes to your head,

428
00:23:16,759 --> 00:23:18,400
leaving little left to help you digest.

429
00:23:18,599 --> 00:23:21,400
What worry could be bigger than your chopsticks?

430
00:23:22,880 --> 00:23:24,480
If you can talk about it, is it really a burden?

431
00:23:26,279 --> 00:23:27,720
Bottling it up will only make it worse.

432
00:23:28,200 --> 00:23:29,599
Let me know if you need anything.

433
00:23:30,240 --> 00:23:30,839
Chief Wei.

434
00:23:31,240 --> 00:23:31,680
Over here.

435
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:40,799
What were you chatting about?

436
00:23:41,160 --> 00:23:42,000
Having such a lively chat.

437
00:23:43,200 --> 00:23:44,400
Neither of you has ever been divorced.

438
00:23:44,799 --> 00:23:46,519
You wouldn't know the joy of freedom.

439
00:23:48,240 --> 00:23:49,559
I can finally work a case alone.

440
00:23:51,119 --> 00:23:52,240
When can I report over there?

441
00:23:52,400 --> 00:23:53,720
Why are you in such a hurry to leave?

442
00:23:54,359 --> 00:23:55,519
I'll try my best not to drop the ball in the future.

443
00:23:55,880 --> 00:23:56,880
It's my own lack of ability.

444
00:23:56,880 --> 00:23:57,559
I can't teach you.

445
00:23:57,839 --> 00:23:58,799
No, no, no.

446
00:23:58,799 --> 00:24:00,000
It's me. I'm too incompetent.

447
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:01,240
Always dragging you down.

448
00:24:04,160 --> 00:24:04,880
Just look.

449
00:24:05,640 --> 00:24:07,720
Tailing Lin Kanshan, chasing Wen Zongshu...

450
00:24:07,720 --> 00:24:09,119
including the mailman from the very start.

451
00:24:09,200 --> 00:24:11,160
Not a single screw-up happened without you involved.

452
00:24:11,880 --> 00:24:13,079
See, you're the one saying it.

453
00:24:14,079 --> 00:24:14,960
To be completely fair,

454
00:24:15,079 --> 00:24:16,799
you really aren't as capable as Huadong.

455
00:24:16,799 --> 00:24:17,400
But when it comes to luck,

456
00:24:17,400 --> 00:24:18,079
he can't beat you.

457
00:24:18,200 --> 00:24:19,440
Frankly, I think

458
00:24:19,640 --> 00:24:21,319
wiretapping with Jinlan suits you just fine.

459
00:24:22,119 --> 00:24:23,119
That's for later.

460
00:24:23,759 --> 00:24:25,400
At least with the assignment at hand,

461
00:24:25,880 --> 00:24:26,799
I'm seeing it through to the end.

462
00:24:28,160 --> 00:24:29,160
Follow through if you want. It's up to you.

463
00:24:29,440 --> 00:24:30,519
Just don't follow me.

464
00:24:36,559 --> 00:24:38,559
The mailman, Lin Kanshan, Wen Zongshu...

465
00:24:38,559 --> 00:24:39,599
I've been following your lead all along.

466
00:24:39,880 --> 00:24:41,000
And to be completely fair myself,

467
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:41,839
I think on certain things,

468
00:24:41,839 --> 00:24:43,359
you were actually the one who misjudged.

469
00:24:43,599 --> 00:24:44,160
You're not a god.

470
00:24:44,160 --> 00:24:44,960
You're only human.

471
00:24:44,960 --> 00:24:46,880
Humans make mistakes and have weaknesses.

472
00:24:46,880 --> 00:24:48,559
Of course I have them too, even more so.

473
00:24:49,000 --> 00:24:50,839
But at least I don't give up halfway.

474
00:24:53,559 --> 00:24:54,440
Blind confidence.

475
00:24:54,440 --> 00:24:55,559
What're you relying on not to fail?

476
00:24:55,680 --> 00:24:56,640
I have no selfish motives.

477
00:24:57,000 --> 00:24:57,680
That's what I'm relying on.

478
00:24:57,799 --> 00:24:58,720
Turning your partner into your wife...

479
00:24:58,720 --> 00:24:59,480
You call that having no selfish motives?

480
00:24:59,480 --> 00:25:01,640
Even when our child is born, I won't back out.

481
00:25:03,000 --> 00:25:05,039
If you keep meddling and blow this,

482
00:25:05,519 --> 00:25:06,640
can you handle the fallout?

483
00:25:06,640 --> 00:25:07,759
If I can handle the fallout, I will.

484
00:25:07,759 --> 00:25:09,160
If not, the worst that happens is I get reassigned.

485
00:25:09,160 --> 00:25:10,119
I'll follow leadership's orders.

486
00:25:14,480 --> 00:25:15,000
Here's what we'll do.

487
00:25:15,519 --> 00:25:16,400
One officer per case.

488
00:25:16,720 --> 00:25:18,559
After A-Cai's interrogation wraps up,

489
00:25:19,559 --> 00:25:20,519
you get your transfer,

490
00:25:21,079 --> 00:25:21,880
and you get reassigned.

491
00:25:22,640 --> 00:25:25,039
Chunxiao will work with Baoshan from now on.

492
00:25:25,920 --> 00:25:26,720
Fine by me.

493
00:25:30,920 --> 00:25:31,960
I'm done eating.

494
00:25:50,039 --> 00:25:50,599
Hello,

495
00:25:50,599 --> 00:25:51,519
everyone.

496
00:25:51,880 --> 00:25:53,000
Our tour bus

497
00:25:53,000 --> 00:25:55,039
has slowly entered Huandao Road,

498
00:25:55,240 --> 00:25:56,119
marking

499
00:25:56,119 --> 00:25:59,599
the official start of our Xiamen tour.

500
00:25:59,599 --> 00:26:00,839
All right.

501
00:26:00,839 --> 00:26:02,200
At this very moment,

502
00:26:02,480 --> 00:26:04,599
I'd like to use three words to summarize

503
00:26:04,599 --> 00:26:06,759
this time we are spending together.

504
00:26:06,759 --> 00:26:08,759
The first word is "affinity."

505
00:26:09,119 --> 00:26:10,359
As the old saying goes,

506
00:26:10,359 --> 00:26:12,200
"It takes a century of cultivation to cross on the same boat,

507
00:26:12,200 --> 00:26:14,559
and a millennium to share a pillow."

508
00:26:14,559 --> 00:26:17,279
Our gathering right here, right now,

509
00:26:17,279 --> 00:26:18,960
feels like centuries of destined connection

510
00:26:18,960 --> 00:26:21,079
culminating at this very moment.

511
00:26:21,079 --> 00:26:22,799
You can take this natural balm inside

512
00:26:23,079 --> 00:26:25,160
and rub it behind your ears or on your temples.

513
00:26:25,160 --> 00:26:26,119
It'll make you feel much better.

514
00:26:26,119 --> 00:26:28,480
None of this would be possible without your support

515
00:26:28,480 --> 00:26:29,359
and cooperation.

516
00:26:29,359 --> 00:26:31,279
I sincerely thank you all.

517
00:26:31,599 --> 00:26:34,240
And the final word sounds the same—"wealth."

518
00:26:34,359 --> 00:26:36,480
May you all amass great fortune,

519
00:26:36,480 --> 00:26:38,319
flowing endlessly like a river.

520
00:26:38,759 --> 00:26:40,319
Okay, okay.

521
00:26:40,599 --> 00:26:41,440
People in the back, keep up!

522
00:26:41,440 --> 00:26:42,839
Have your IDs ready.

523
00:26:44,000 --> 00:26:45,039
Come on, this way.

524
00:26:45,039 --> 00:26:46,599
To the right. Follow me.

525
00:26:47,920 --> 00:26:49,920
Head inside. Head inside first.

526
00:26:50,519 --> 00:26:51,720
Stop taking photos for now.

527
00:26:51,720 --> 00:26:53,039
This way.

528
00:26:53,039 --> 00:26:53,880
Keep moving inside.

529
00:26:53,880 --> 00:26:55,319
Xiaoxue, we're here. Shenzhou's group.

530
00:26:55,319 --> 00:26:56,200
Checking in.

531
00:26:56,400 --> 00:26:57,319
In pairs of two.

532
00:26:57,880 --> 00:26:59,480
Roommates, register together.

533
00:26:59,480 --> 00:27:00,759
Have your IDs ready.

534
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:02,400
Anyone else in the back? In the back?

535
00:27:02,400 --> 00:27:03,960
Xiaoxue, help me check in, will you?

536
00:27:05,079 --> 00:27:06,359
Step forward, step forward.

537
00:27:06,640 --> 00:27:08,240
Everyone, please step forward a bit.

538
00:27:08,240 --> 00:27:09,759
After upgrading with a gold membership card,

539
00:27:09,759 --> 00:27:10,839
your room type can also be upgraded.

540
00:27:10,839 --> 00:27:12,279
But there are no king rooms left.

541
00:27:12,440 --> 00:27:13,680
What did you say? I didn't catch that.

542
00:27:13,680 --> 00:27:15,079
We're running low on rooms right now.

543
00:27:15,079 --> 00:27:16,160
Would a standard twin room be okay?

544
00:27:16,400 --> 00:27:17,000
That works.

545
00:27:17,160 --> 00:27:18,799
I'll share with that girl in a bit.

546
00:27:19,839 --> 00:27:20,279
All right.

547
00:27:20,279 --> 00:27:21,839
Go rest in your rooms first.

548
00:27:21,839 --> 00:27:23,599
Meal times will be arranged together.

549
00:27:24,759 --> 00:27:25,759
Okay, thank you.

550
00:28:27,279 --> 00:28:29,000
I spend half the year living in hotels,

551
00:28:29,440 --> 00:28:31,119
so every hotel has my information.

552
00:28:31,599 --> 00:28:33,359
A lot of people turn around and sell your number.

553
00:28:33,519 --> 00:28:34,440
If I use a fake name,

554
00:28:34,440 --> 00:28:35,960
at least I know which one did it.

555
00:29:03,279 --> 00:29:05,000
Am I still two-fifty short?

556
00:29:05,680 --> 00:29:05,799
Yes.

557
00:29:05,799 --> 00:29:06,920
Then I'll get shredded potatoes.

558
00:29:07,240 --> 00:29:08,039
Does that put me over?

559
00:29:09,400 --> 00:29:10,960
Let me look again. Let me see.

560
00:29:11,480 --> 00:29:12,839
The potatoes put you over by one-fifty.

561
00:29:13,599 --> 00:29:15,319
Reimbursement won't care if I'm only over by a yuan.

562
00:29:15,319 --> 00:29:16,960
It's not about whether I pay the difference.

563
00:29:16,960 --> 00:29:18,240
I can't account for it when I get back.

564
00:29:18,240 --> 00:29:19,039
How about this?

565
00:29:19,160 --> 00:29:21,759
Just add anything you want.

566
00:29:22,400 --> 00:29:23,200
Herbal tea,

567
00:29:23,400 --> 00:29:24,119
or whatever else.

568
00:29:24,119 --> 00:29:24,799
Help me round it out.

569
00:29:24,799 --> 00:29:25,160
Sure.

570
00:29:25,160 --> 00:29:25,640
Thanks.

571
00:29:31,759 --> 00:29:33,359
Do you like crosswords?

572
00:29:33,920 --> 00:29:35,240
I've been hooked on them lately.

573
00:29:35,359 --> 00:29:36,400
I need to take this back later.

574
00:29:36,599 --> 00:29:38,319
I'm no good at anything that takes too much thinking.

575
00:29:38,839 --> 00:29:40,119
Listening to pop songs is more my thing.

576
00:29:41,039 --> 00:29:43,279
I remember on your resume for the agency,

577
00:29:43,279 --> 00:29:45,279
you said you'd published poetry before.

578
00:29:45,279 --> 00:29:46,640
Do you still write?

579
00:29:47,319 --> 00:29:48,599
A busy person like me?

580
00:29:49,000 --> 00:29:50,359
Where would I find the time for poetry?

581
00:29:51,680 --> 00:29:52,680
I stopped a long time ago.

582
00:29:56,039 --> 00:29:57,640
Where was your first piece published?

583
00:29:58,240 --> 00:29:59,519
Campus Literature?

584
00:29:59,759 --> 00:30:00,920
That was way too hard.

585
00:30:01,440 --> 00:30:02,640
Just Buds.

586
00:30:02,640 --> 00:30:03,799
A small magazine.

587
00:30:07,519 --> 00:30:09,759
A supplement of Yellow River Literature, right?

588
00:30:11,359 --> 00:30:12,319
You know it?

589
00:30:13,559 --> 00:30:14,960
I submitted work there, too.

590
00:30:15,079 --> 00:30:16,720
In the third issue of 1999,

591
00:30:16,720 --> 00:30:18,359
they published a prose poem of mine.

592
00:30:18,359 --> 00:30:19,480
Which year and issue were you?

593
00:30:19,480 --> 00:30:21,039
It can't be that much of a coincidence.

594
00:30:21,200 --> 00:30:22,359
Mine was in 1999, too.

595
00:30:22,519 --> 00:30:24,200
But I've kind of forgotten which issue.

596
00:30:24,440 --> 00:30:25,640
In "Poetry Corner,"

597
00:30:25,640 --> 00:30:27,640
two of the four poems were mine.

598
00:30:27,759 --> 00:30:29,039
My pen name was Autumn.

599
00:30:29,119 --> 00:30:29,920
What was yours?

600
00:30:30,119 --> 00:30:31,359
Just Jinlan.

601
00:30:31,519 --> 00:30:32,480
Back then, they even gave me

602
00:30:32,480 --> 00:30:33,880
30 yuan in royalties.

603
00:30:34,160 --> 00:30:35,160
Two ten-yuan bills,

604
00:30:35,160 --> 00:30:36,119
two five-yuan bills.

605
00:30:36,119 --> 00:30:37,799
Even now, they're still under the glass

606
00:30:37,799 --> 00:30:39,680
on the desk at my mom's place.

607
00:30:40,200 --> 00:30:41,799
Have you ever read Juvenile Literature?

608
00:30:41,960 --> 00:30:43,119
I've only ever published one poem.

609
00:30:43,119 --> 00:30:44,839
Very short, and published right there.

610
00:30:45,839 --> 00:30:46,480
So,

611
00:30:47,400 --> 00:30:48,799
who's your favorite poet?

612
00:30:51,039 --> 00:30:51,960
Let me guess.

613
00:30:52,240 --> 00:30:53,160
Is it Xi Murong?

614
00:30:54,480 --> 00:30:55,440
Why guess her?

615
00:30:55,440 --> 00:30:56,440
Why not Shu Ting?

616
00:30:57,799 --> 00:30:58,680
Intuition.

617
00:30:59,079 --> 00:31:00,240
Just like writing poetry.

618
00:31:01,440 --> 00:31:03,039
I bet you don't like Misty Poetry.

619
00:31:03,759 --> 00:31:05,920
Weeping on a lover's shoulder...

620
00:31:06,920 --> 00:31:08,119
I don't think you're that kind of person.

621
00:31:09,680 --> 00:31:10,839
Hello, excuse me.

622
00:31:16,039 --> 00:31:16,839
Please enjoy your meal.

623
00:31:25,839 --> 00:31:26,960
What do you want me to do?

624
00:31:27,480 --> 00:31:29,519
It's been so long. Why haven't you said anything?

625
00:31:33,079 --> 00:31:33,880
Nothing.

626
00:31:37,200 --> 00:31:38,440
At least, not right now.

627
00:31:50,680 --> 00:31:51,480
What's wrong?

628
00:31:52,640 --> 00:31:53,640
Nothing.

629
00:31:58,319 --> 00:31:59,599
What were you about to say?

630
00:32:03,079 --> 00:32:05,839
Whose hand suddenly drew back,

631
00:32:07,119 --> 00:32:08,920
only to tightly cover their eyes?

632
00:32:10,720 --> 00:32:11,920
Shu Ting writes so beautifully.

633
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:21,279
What's wrong?

634
00:33:25,359 --> 00:33:26,319
Are you okay?

635
00:33:26,480 --> 00:33:27,359
What happened?

636
00:33:39,000 --> 00:33:40,440
It's always in the middle of the night.

637
00:33:40,440 --> 00:33:42,720
It gets so bad I can barely breathe.

638
00:33:46,839 --> 00:33:47,960
I can't speak.

639
00:33:47,960 --> 00:33:49,559
My hands and feet are ice-cold.

640
00:33:49,839 --> 00:33:50,839
I still haven't recovered.

641
00:33:51,000 --> 00:33:52,000
The ECG is normal.

642
00:33:52,359 --> 00:33:53,519
The echocardiogram is fine, too.

643
00:33:53,519 --> 00:33:55,799
Why not visit Building 3 during the day?

644
00:33:55,960 --> 00:33:57,160
What's in Building 3?

645
00:33:57,319 --> 00:33:58,000
Psychiatry.

646
00:34:07,519 --> 00:34:08,679
Look outside.

647
00:34:10,559 --> 00:34:11,440
It's almost dawn.

648
00:34:26,199 --> 00:34:28,039
Don't dwell on the bad things.

649
00:34:34,639 --> 00:34:35,199
Listen to me.

650
00:34:35,199 --> 00:34:37,360
We need to find a way to distract you.

651
00:34:38,760 --> 00:34:40,199
Think about your childhood.

652
00:34:41,159 --> 00:34:42,679
Think about the poems you love.

653
00:34:43,599 --> 00:34:45,400
"I am the last traveler on your road,

654
00:34:45,400 --> 00:34:46,599
I am on your road,

655
00:34:46,599 --> 00:34:47,920
the last spring,

656
00:34:48,079 --> 00:34:49,679
the last traveler,

657
00:34:50,079 --> 00:34:51,800
the last spring,

658
00:34:54,880 --> 00:34:56,280
the last snow,

659
00:34:59,599 --> 00:35:03,079
the last battle for survival.

660
00:35:04,840 --> 00:35:05,639
Look.

661
00:35:06,719 --> 00:35:08,599
We are lower than ever,

662
00:35:10,400 --> 00:35:11,920
and higher than ever.

663
00:35:15,519 --> 00:35:17,880
In our fire, there is everything.

664
00:35:20,320 --> 00:35:21,400
There are pine cones,

665
00:35:24,119 --> 00:35:25,280
vine branches,

666
00:35:28,199 --> 00:35:30,440
flowers lovelier than running water,

667
00:35:32,239 --> 00:35:33,280
mud,

668
00:35:34,920 --> 00:35:35,960
and dew drops.

669
00:35:37,159 --> 00:35:39,039
Beneath our feet is fire,

670
00:35:39,679 --> 00:35:41,360
and above fire is fire.

671
00:35:42,440 --> 00:35:43,239
Insects,

672
00:35:44,760 --> 00:35:46,039
birds,

673
00:35:46,880 --> 00:35:47,840
and men

674
00:35:50,239 --> 00:35:52,679
will all take flight from beneath our feet.

675
00:35:56,360 --> 00:35:57,440
And those in flight

676
00:35:59,079 --> 00:36:00,760
are about to land."

677
00:36:13,599 --> 00:36:15,400
The sky is clear,

678
00:36:16,679 --> 00:36:18,079
the earth is gloomy.

679
00:36:21,639 --> 00:36:23,400
Flames remain in the world.

680
00:36:24,559 --> 00:36:26,760
Flames are the clouds of the soul.

681
00:36:27,800 --> 00:36:31,679
Flames are all the tributaries of blood.

682
00:36:32,679 --> 00:36:34,559
It sings our tune.

683
00:36:36,199 --> 00:36:38,760
It dispels our winter dampness.

684
00:36:41,119 --> 00:36:42,320
Medication for life...

685
00:36:44,280 --> 00:36:45,880
Won't that kill me?

686
00:36:46,320 --> 00:36:47,079
Doctor,

687
00:36:47,360 --> 00:36:49,480
can I just take half a pill each time?

688
00:36:50,960 --> 00:36:52,760
You can't reduce the dose or stop taking it.

689
00:36:52,760 --> 00:36:54,119
Pick up your medicine at the first-floor pharmacy.

690
00:36:54,519 --> 00:36:55,320
Take this with you too.

691
00:36:58,159 --> 00:36:59,440
Any other questions?

692
00:37:01,039 --> 00:37:01,800
Then you can head out.

693
00:37:03,119 --> 00:37:04,039
Thank you, Doctor.

694
00:37:04,360 --> 00:37:04,920
Alright.

695
00:37:10,039 --> 00:37:10,840
Jinlan,

696
00:37:11,559 --> 00:37:14,039
I have a favor to ask.

697
00:37:14,840 --> 00:37:17,679
Could you please not tell the travel agency,

698
00:37:18,000 --> 00:37:19,480
and don't tell the manager either?

699
00:38:00,760 --> 00:38:01,599
It's so hot.

700
00:38:01,840 --> 00:38:03,320
Officer Ma, what a coincidence.

701
00:38:07,119 --> 00:38:08,880
That's how fake hot springs are.

702
00:38:14,360 --> 00:38:15,960
You told me to keep an eye on Wen Zongshu.

703
00:38:15,960 --> 00:38:17,159
I've been doing that all along.

704
00:38:18,559 --> 00:38:20,960
I just haven't seen much of him lately.

705
00:38:21,320 --> 00:38:22,360
I've been traveling for business constantly.

706
00:38:22,800 --> 00:38:24,159
The new factory was just set up,

707
00:38:24,159 --> 00:38:24,760
so there's a lot on my plate.

708
00:38:24,760 --> 00:38:25,519
Shut it down.

709
00:38:26,000 --> 00:38:27,000
Being a boss is exhausting.

710
00:38:27,000 --> 00:38:28,199
And you don't even make much money.

711
00:38:29,880 --> 00:38:32,320
Did I do something to offend you?

712
00:38:32,320 --> 00:38:33,880
Or did I mess something up?

713
00:38:33,880 --> 00:38:35,199
Just tell me straight.

714
00:38:35,199 --> 00:38:36,199
We're all busy.

715
00:38:36,440 --> 00:38:36,920
Let's not beat around the bush.

716
00:38:37,000 --> 00:38:38,000
Let's keep it simple.

717
00:38:38,880 --> 00:38:40,360
The land where you built your factory

718
00:38:40,360 --> 00:38:41,800
was originally allocated to Lin Kanshan.

719
00:38:42,000 --> 00:38:43,119
We should be reasonable about this.

720
00:38:43,920 --> 00:38:44,559
Here's what you do:

721
00:38:44,840 --> 00:38:46,920
transfer the factory, staff, and equipment to him.

722
00:38:47,039 --> 00:38:49,000
As for the exact price, he'll discuss it with you later.

723
00:38:49,400 --> 00:38:50,360
A friendly cooperation.

724
00:38:55,840 --> 00:38:56,880
Frankly speaking,

725
00:38:57,760 --> 00:38:59,280
I'm not the only shareholder.

726
00:39:00,599 --> 00:39:02,000
What if I can't do that?

727
00:39:07,639 --> 00:39:09,639
Intentional injury, endangering state security,

728
00:39:09,760 --> 00:39:10,519
brawling,

729
00:39:10,519 --> 00:39:11,519
soliciting prostitution, gambling...

730
00:39:11,519 --> 00:39:13,000
Combined punishment for multiple offenses.

731
00:39:13,800 --> 00:39:14,800
If you can't do it,

732
00:39:14,800 --> 00:39:15,800
then I'll take care of it.

733
00:39:16,320 --> 00:39:17,039
Shut down the factory.

734
00:39:17,639 --> 00:39:18,320
Right away.

735
00:39:49,360 --> 00:39:50,800
Thanks for your help these past few days.

736
00:39:57,320 --> 00:39:58,039
Come on in.

737
00:39:59,920 --> 00:40:01,559
Xiaolin, I'm back.

738
00:40:06,719 --> 00:40:07,559
Xiaolin?

739
00:40:12,400 --> 00:40:13,199
Xiaolin!

740
00:40:17,679 --> 00:40:18,360
Xiaolin?

741
00:40:22,599 --> 00:40:23,320
Xiaolin!

742
00:40:30,639 --> 00:40:31,280
Xiaolin.

743
00:40:37,480 --> 00:40:38,199
Xiaolin?

744
00:40:45,599 --> 00:40:46,440
Xiaolin!

745
00:40:48,199 --> 00:40:51,159
Xiaolin! Xiaolin, Xiaolin!

746
00:40:52,519 --> 00:40:53,320
Xiaolin!

747
00:40:54,159 --> 00:40:56,360
Xiaolin, Xiaolin.

748
00:40:57,920 --> 00:41:00,400
Xiaolin, Xiaolin!

749
00:41:02,280 --> 00:41:02,920
Xiaolin!

750
00:41:06,239 --> 00:41:06,880
Xiaolin!

751
00:41:07,199 --> 00:41:07,960
It's okay, don't worry.

752
00:41:08,239 --> 00:41:09,400
It couldn't have gone far.

753
00:41:09,480 --> 00:41:11,119
Cats always find their way home.

754
00:41:12,440 --> 00:41:13,079
Really.

755
00:41:14,119 --> 00:41:14,840
It's all right.

756
00:41:15,480 --> 00:41:16,559
I'll help you look.

757
00:41:24,719 --> 00:41:26,159
When in Rome, do as the Romans do.

758
00:41:26,880 --> 00:41:28,679
You need to learn mainland laws.

759
00:41:29,159 --> 00:41:30,599
Getting into a brawl is one thing.

760
00:41:30,599 --> 00:41:31,719
At most, it's just fighting.

761
00:41:32,599 --> 00:41:34,000
Worst case, you could settle it privately.

762
00:41:34,960 --> 00:41:36,639
Yet you had to bang on his door at midnight for revenge,

763
00:41:37,239 --> 00:41:39,639
making him call the police and nearly hitting the news.

764
00:41:39,639 --> 00:41:40,920
Aren't you afraid of blowing your cover?

765
00:41:41,840 --> 00:41:43,320
It was such a petty thing.

766
00:41:43,440 --> 00:41:44,840
I never expected it to turn out like this.

767
00:41:44,920 --> 00:41:46,519
He claimed he had intel to sell,

768
00:41:46,760 --> 00:41:49,119
then pulled a badger game to extort me in person.

769
00:41:49,119 --> 00:41:50,159
He took me for a fool.

770
00:41:50,719 --> 00:41:52,360
Who could swallow that?

771
00:41:54,320 --> 00:41:56,320
Every time you can't handle the fallout, you come running to me.

772
00:41:57,039 --> 00:41:58,039
Let's see what we can do.

773
00:41:58,960 --> 00:42:00,760
Hand everything over to the lawyer,

774
00:42:01,000 --> 00:42:02,360
and lay low in Guangdong for a couple of days.

775
00:42:03,320 --> 00:42:03,920
Also,

776
00:42:03,920 --> 00:42:05,239
hurry up and take down

777
00:42:05,239 --> 00:42:06,079
that lousy blog of yours.

778
00:42:06,519 --> 00:42:08,679
The internet is full of cynical nobodies.

779
00:42:08,840 --> 00:42:10,280
Do you really think you can catch any big fish?

780
00:42:10,559 --> 00:42:12,199
That depends on luck.

781
00:42:12,559 --> 00:42:14,119
Just last month, a big fish

782
00:42:14,360 --> 00:42:16,239
went around emailing people on his own.

783
00:42:16,440 --> 00:42:18,280
You wouldn't believe it if I told you.

784
00:42:21,519 --> 00:42:22,639
Taipei pays generous money.

785
00:42:23,199 --> 00:42:24,920
Either US dollars or little gold Buddhas.

786
00:42:25,159 --> 00:42:26,079
He spends lavishly.

787
00:42:26,519 --> 00:42:27,519
Even I was tempted.

788
00:42:33,719 --> 00:42:36,280
Boss Zhu said he was being too vulgar,

789
00:42:36,800 --> 00:42:37,880
worrying he wasn't showing enough courtesy.

790
00:42:38,880 --> 00:42:40,400
He has truly admired you from afar for a long time,

791
00:42:40,400 --> 00:42:41,400
and just wants to meet you.

792
00:42:44,480 --> 00:42:46,440
When the time comes, we will meet naturally.

793
00:42:47,199 --> 00:42:48,119
Let's leave it to fate.

794
00:42:51,400 --> 00:42:52,559
Such a huge appetite.

795
00:42:57,079 --> 00:42:58,360
Just take the bait already.

796
00:43:08,480 --> 00:43:09,559
I'm Wang Kai,

797
00:43:09,559 --> 00:43:11,280
inviting you to watch the drama

798
00:43:11,280 --> 00:43:12,119
*Confrontation*.

799
00:43:14,039 --> 00:43:14,880
Where have you been,

800
00:43:14,880 --> 00:43:15,920
looking like such a mess?

801
00:43:16,119 --> 00:43:17,239
I was tailing someone.

802
00:43:17,239 --> 00:43:18,159
Did it have to be today?

803
00:43:18,159 --> 00:43:20,360
No choice. He picked today.

804
00:43:20,360 --> 00:43:22,599
Meeting in the rain leaves no traces.

805
00:43:26,559 --> 00:43:27,719
I'm asking you one last time.

806
00:43:27,880 --> 00:43:29,079
Are you going to talk or not?

807
00:43:31,920 --> 00:43:32,800
Where is Ma Qi?

808
00:43:33,000 --> 00:43:33,960
Has he lost his mind?

809
00:43:33,960 --> 00:43:35,599
Do you have anything else to say?

810
00:43:35,599 --> 00:43:37,000
I want to submit my resignation.

811
00:43:37,000 --> 00:43:38,000
I ask the organization for approval.
